      ":question/problem": "Consider the recurrence relation\n$a_{n + 1} = a_{n} + 2, a_{1} = 5, n \u2208 N$.\n\nSuppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n$a_{n} = 2n + 3$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n = 1$:$2(3) + 1$ {{field-1}} **Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n =$ {{field-2}}, we have\n$2k + 3$ {{field-3}} **Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n$2k + 4$ {{field-4}} **Conclusion**: Therefore, $a_{n} = 2n + 3$ for all $n \u2208 N$."
